# Working notes for whoever is editing this, and whatever their tooling
# leaves behind. Neither is part of the software.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.playwright-mcp/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Reference databases pulled off the live instance. Real measurements,
# several megabytes, and reproducible with tools/pull-reference.sh.
/reference/
# Anything that is a credential. The listener's upload token, the settings
# page's token, and whatever the compose file reads out of .env. These decide
# who can write to the archive and who can point it at a different file, so
# they are named individually rather than trusted to a pattern.
deploy/.token
deploy/.admin-token
deploy/.env
deploy/*.env
!deploy/.env.example
*.token
!tools/*.token

# The Caddy site file: it names a real host and this repository does not.
deploy/weewx-evo.caddy

# What a running instance produced. Configuration is per-installation and
# the databases are the installation.
/data/
*.sdb
*.sdb-shm
*.sdb-wal
evo.toml
plots.toml
*.bak
*.part

# A pattern without a slash matches at every level, and one of those levels
# is the source tree: `plots.toml` above was written for the running
# installation's file and quietly took the starter set with it. A fresh
# clone had no charts, and nothing said so -- `is_starter()` answers True
# for a file that is not there, which is right for an installation and
# indistinguishable from this.
!src/weewx_evo/starter/plots.toml

# Screenshots taken while working on the settings page. Two have gone in
# by accident; the page is checked by looking at it, and what is looked at
# is not what is kept.
*.png
!src/**/*.png
!.charts/*.png
